---
// Coverage paths — three tall tinted tiles, each with its own CTA button.
// The buttons are outline capsules, not gold: gold stays reserved for the
// primary actions (call Lisa, get help), and three gold pills in one row would
// flatten that hierarchy. No prices anywhere.
//
// Three squares only. Life, cancer, heart-attack and stroke cover came off this
// row — the site sells three things properly rather than eight vaguely, and each
// tile now points at a real page instead of an anchor further down this one.
//
// No arrow glyphs in the labels: the self-hosted Open Sans is a latin subset
// with no U+2191/U+2193, so they rendered as missing-glyph boxes.
---

<section class="section" id="coverage" aria-labelledby="coverage-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Coverage</p>

    <div class="section-intro">
      <h2 id="coverage-heading">What I can help you with.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="cards cards--3 cards--tiles">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Medicare</h3>
        <p>Together, we’ll review your doctors and prescriptions to find the Medicare coverage that’s right for you.</p>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/medicare">About Medicare</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Health Insurance</h3>
        <p>The right option depends on where you are right now. Marketplace coverage fits many individuals and families under 65, and a short-term plan can cover a gap between one plan ending and the next beginning.</p>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/health-insurance">About health insurance</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Dental &amp; Vision</h3>
        <p>Standalone plans you can start at any time of the year, whether you’re currently on Medicare or not.</p>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/dental-insurance">About dental &amp; vision</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
